# Generalized Born beyond D144 (D152), on the peptide of
# generalized-born.test: the model of Hawkins, Cramer, and Truhlar
# (`implicit_solvent = "HCT"`), a salt that screens the solvent
# (`salt_concentration`, mol/L, at the temperature of [ensemble]), the
# integral of the descreening cut at `born_radius_cutoff`, and the radii of
# mbondi2 by element (`born_radii = "MBONDI2"`). check_born.py computes each
# from the formulas, and the forces against central differences. The radii
# of mbondi2 are those of the topology, built with mbondi2: the same
# energies. Then the peptide from a topology of GROMACS that ParmEd wrote,
# whose coordinates are rounded to 0.001 nm, with the radii of mbondi2: the
# energies of the topology of Amber at those coordinates, and the forces of
# generalized Born within 1e-8, the charges of the file having eight
# decimals. Then the errors.
#
# REQUIRES: hdf5
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/gb/peptide.prmtop %S/Inputs/gb/peptide.inpcrd %S/Inputs/gb/peptide-rounded.inpcrd %S/Inputs/gb/peptide.top %S/Inputs/gb/peptide.gro %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/generalized-born.test | sed '1d;$d' > %t/born.toml
# RUN: sed -e '/^implicit_solvent/d' -e '/^surface_area_energy/d' -e 's/born.h5/plain.h5/' %t/born.toml > %t/plain.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run plain.toml > plain.log
# RUN: mdir checkpoint --print=forces %t/plain.h5 > %t/plain.forces
#
# RUN: sed -e 's/"OBC2"/"HCT"/' -e 's/born.h5/hct.h5/' %t/born.toml > %t/hct.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run hct.toml | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HCT
# RUN: mdir checkpoint --print=forces %t/hct.h5 > %t/hct.forces
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_born.py %t/peptide.prmtop %t/peptide.inpcrd %t/plain.forces %t/hct.forces --model HCT | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HCT-PYTHON
#
